questions.questionText:
Use the following thermochemical data to calculate the magnitude of the lattice enthalpy (in $\text{kJ mol}^{-1}$) of solid magnesium oxide, $\text{MgO}(s)$:
Standard enthalpy of formation of $\text{MgO}(s) = -602\text{ kJ mol}^{-1}$;
Enthalpy of sublimation of $\text{Mg}(s) = +148\text{ kJ mol}^{-1}$;
First and second ionization enthalpies of $\text{Mg}(g) = +738\text{ kJ mol}^{-1}$ and $+1451\text{ kJ mol}^{-1}$;
Bond dissociation enthalpy of $\text{O}_2(g) = +498\text{ kJ mol}^{-1}$;
First electron gain enthalpy of $\text{O}(g) = -141\text{ kJ mol}^{-1}$;
Second electron gain enthalpy of $\text{O}^-(g) = +744\text{ kJ mol}^{-1}$.
